{'symbol': 'LLY', 'date': '2020-08-10 11:30:00', 'title': 'Pieris Pharmaceuticals Inc - Entered Into A Clinical Trial Collaboration And Supply Agreement With Eli Lilly And Co', 'text': 'PIERIS PHARMACEUTICALS INC -  ENTERED INTO A CLINICAL TRIAL COLLABORATION AND SUPPLY AGREEMENT WITH ELI LILLY AND COMPANY.PIERIS PHARMACEUTICALS - CO, LILLY WILL COLLABORATE IN A PHASE 2 CLINICAL STUDY OF PRS-343 WITH RAMUCIRUMAB AND PACLITAXEL, FOR GASTRIC CANCER.PIERIS PHARMACEUTICALS INC - CO SHALL SPONSOR STUDY AND LILLY SHALL SUPPLY PIERIS WITH RAMUCIRUMAB.PIERIS -  LILLY TO PROVIDE INPUT ON SOME ASPECTS OF GASTRIC CANCER STUDY IN EXHANGE FOR JOINTLY OWNING POSSIBLE INVENTIONS FROM COMBINATION REGIMEN.'}
{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2020-08-10 12:30:00', 'title': 'Marriott Sees Slower Cash Burn As Domestic Travel Recovers - Conf Call', 'text': 'MARRIOTT CEO SAYS THERE IS STILL NO VISIBILITY AROUND WHEN REVPAR COULD RETURN TO 2019 LEVELS - CONF. CALL.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS REVPAR DECLINE IN JULY SLOWED TO 70%, FROM 78% IN JUNE AND 85% IN MAY.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS AFTER DECLINING 85% YEAR-OVER-YEAR IN FEBRUARY, REVPAR IN GREATER CHINA IMPROVED TO DOWN 34% IN JULY.MARRIOTT CEO - AT CURRENT RATE OF RECOVERY, ASSUMING NO WIDE RESURGENCE OF COVID-19, GREATER CHINA MARKET COULD APPROACH 2019 OCCUPANCY, REVPAR LEVELS AS EARLY AS NEXT YEAR.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS SYSTEM-WIDE N.AMERICA REVPAR CONTINUED TO IMPROVE IN JULY TO Y-O-Y DECLINE OF 69%, WHICH IS 7 PERCENT POINTS BETTER THAN JUNE.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS EXPECTS "SOLID LEISURE DEMAND" WILL CONTINUE THROUGH LABOR DAY IN NORTH AMERICA.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS EXPECTS "SOLID LEISURE DEMAND" IN NORTH AMERICA COULD CONTINUE INTO THE FALL AS EMPLOYERS & SCHOOLS ALIKE OPERATE REMOTELY.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS BUSINESS TRANSIENT & GROUP DEMAND IN NORTH AMERICA WHILE LAGGING ARE SHOWING VERY EARLY SIGNS OF IMPROVEMENT.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS GROUP BOOKINGS, OUTSIDE OF THOSE ASSOCIATED WITH CO\'S CAREGIVER & FIRST RESPONDER PROGRAMS, TEND TO BE MOSTLY SMALLER ONES.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS YEAR-TO-DATE, HAVE SIGNED 30% MORE DEALS IN ASIA PACIFIC THAN WE DID IN FIRST HALF OF 2019.MARRIOTT CEO SAYS STILL EXPECT SOME OPENINGS WILL BE DELAYED DUE TO SLOWER CONSTRUCTION TIME LINES & SUPPLY CHAIN ISSUES RELATED TO COVID-19.'}
{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2020-08-10 09:30:00', 'title': 'Marriott International Says Q2 Adjusted Loss Per Share $0.64', 'text': "MARRIOTT INTERNATIONAL REPORTS SECOND QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q2 ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE $0.64.Q2 LOSS PER SHARE $0.72.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $-0.42 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.MARRIOTT - Q2 2020 COMPARABLE SYSTEMWIDE CONSTANT DOLLAR REVPAR DECLINED 84.4 PERCENT WORLDWIDE, 83.6 PERCENT IN NORTH AMERICA.MARRIOTT - Q2 2020 COMPARABLE SYSTEMWIDE CONSTANT DOLLAR REVPAR DECLINED 84.4 PERCENT WORLDWIDE.MARRIOTT - NET LIQUIDITY WAS APPROXIMATELY $4.4 BILLION AS OF END OF Q2.MARRIOTT - EXPECTS THAT COVID-19 WILL CONTINUE TO BE MATERIAL TO COMPANY'S RESULTS.MARRIOTT - QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES $1,464 MILLION VERSUS $5,305 MILLION.MARRIOTT - WORLDWIDE OCCUPANCY RATES, WHICH BOTTOMED AT 11% FOR WEEK ENDED APRIL 11, IMPROVED EACH WEEK, REACHING NEARLY 34% FOR WEEK ENDED AUGUST 1.MARRIOTT - EXPECTS THAT COVID-19 WILL CONTINUE TO BE MATERIAL TO COMPANY'S RESULTS.MARRIOTT - AS OF EARLY MAY, ALL OUR HOTELS IN GREATER CHINA ARE OPEN, AND OCCUPANCY LEVELS ARE NOW REACHING 60%.MARRIOTT - SUSPENDED ITS QUARTERLY DIVIDEND BEGINNING IN Q2.MARRIOTT - ESTIMATE ROOMS COULD GROW BY 2 TO 3 PERCENT, NET, FOR FULL YEAR."}
