{'symbol': 'RCL', 'date': '2020-08-10 10:30:00', 'title': 'Royal Caribbean Reports Q2 Adjusted Loss Per Share $6.13', 'text': 'ROYAL CARIBBEAN GROUP PROVIDES BUSINESS UPDATE AND REPORTS ON SECOND QUARTER 2020.Q2 ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE $6.13.GAAP NET LOSS FOR Q2 OF 2020 $7.83 PER SHARE.ROYAL CARIBBEAN CRUISES - ESTIMATES CASH BURN TO BE, ON AVERAGE, IN RANGE OF ABOUT $250 MILLION TO $290 MILLION/MONTH DURING PROLONGED SUSPENSION OF OPERATIONS.AS OF JUNE 30, 2020, HAD LIQUIDITY OF APPROXIMATELY $4.1 BILLION ALL IN FORM OF CASH AND CASH EQUIVALENTS.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUE $175.6 MILLION VERSUS $2.81 BILLION.EXPECTED CAPITAL EXPENDITURES FOR REMAINDER OF 2020 AND 2021 ARE $0.6 BILLION AND $1.8 BILLION, RESPECTIVELY.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $-4.82, REVENUE VIEW $43.5 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.COVID-19 HAS IMPACTED SHIPYARD OPERATIONS AND WILL RESULT IN DELIVERY DELAYS FOR NEWBUILDS.EXPECTS TO INCUR A NET LOSS ON BOTH A US GAAP AND ADJUSTED BASIS FOR ITS Q3 AND 2020 FISCAL YEAR.INTEREST EXPENSE FOR REMAINDER OF YEAR (JULY 1, 2020 THROUGH DECEMBER 31, 2020) WILL BE IN RANGE OF $505 MILLION TO $515 MILLION.ROYAL CARIBBEAN - SEES 3 OF 5 SHIPS ORIGINALLY SCHEDULED FOR DELIVERY BETWEEN JULY 2020 & DEC 2021 TO BE DELIVERED WITHIN REMAINING TIME FRAME.ROYAL CARIBBEAN CRUISES - AS OF JUNE 30, 2020, HEDGED ABOUT 64%, 40%, 23%, 5% OF PROJECTED METRIC TONS OF FUEL CONSUMPTION FOR REMAINDER OF 2020, 2021, 2022, 2023.NET LOSS FOR QUARTER IS A RESULT OF IMPACT OF COVID-19 PANDEMIC ON BUSINESS.'}
